      "title": "Note: MiniMax H3",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MiniMax H3\n\n[MiniMax H3](https://www.minimax.io/blog/minimax-h3) is MiniMax's general-purpose, omni-modal generation model. It jointly understands text, image, video, and audio, and generates video with **native stereo audio**: voice, sound effects, and music are modeled jointly in a single forward pass, not layered on afterward. Output is up to 2K resolution, 24fps, and up to about 15 seconds per single generation call.\n\n## Links\n- [MiniMax H3 on Hugging Face](https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3)\n- [\ud83e\udd17 Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3 (ComfyUI-ready weights)](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3)\n- [Muse Minimax Director on GitHub](https://github.com/muse-collective-26/MiniMaxH3-Director)\n- [MiniMax H3 official prompt-writing guide](https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3/blob/main/docs/VIDEO_PROMPT_WRITING_GUIDE_ref_en.md)\n\n## About this workflow\n\nThis workflow runs MiniMax H3's **reference-to-video (ref2va)** task through **Muse Minimax Director**, a timeline-based director node that sits on top of the stock `MiniMaxH3ReferenceToVideo` node. Instead of manually writing `<Picture N>` / `<Video N>` / `<Audio N>` tags into a single prompt box, you build a script visually:\n\n- Drop up to 9 character images into **Ref 1-9** and a **Location** image, write a description for each (or click **Analyze**)\n- Write your script as a sequence of **CUTs** along the timeline, and tick who's speaking on each one\n- Optionally add reference video and reference audio - Ref Audio N automatically becomes Ref N's voice\n\nMuse Minimax Director compiles all of that into MiniMax H3's own official reference-mode prompt format - six sections (`subject_definitions`, `summary`, `retention_analysis`, `detailed_description`, `overall_soundscape`, `non_diegetic_music`), with every `<Subject N>` / `<Picture N>` / `<Video N>` / `<Audio N>` tag numbered exactly the way H3 itself assigns them, and long scripts automatically split into multiple chunks if they exceed a single ~15 second generation call. Check the node's `compiled_prompt` output any time you want to see exactly what was sent to H3.\n\n**Sampling**: `res_multistep` sampler; `beta` or `normal` scheduler tends to outperform `simple` for reference-heavy prompts like this one.\n\nFull documentation: [github.com/muse-collective-26/MiniMaxH3-Director](https://github.com/muse-collective-26/MiniMaxH3-Director)"
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
